# Generated output — rebuilt from scratch on every run of site_generate.
# _site/ is the site, _site_drafts/ a --drafts preview, _site_report/ the build
# report. <folder>.tmp/ is where a build is staged before it replaces the
# folder, and <folder>.previous/ holds the old copy for the moment the swap
# takes; neither should survive a finished build, but an interrupted one can
# leave them.
_site/
_site.tmp/
_site.previous/
_site_drafts/
_site_drafts.tmp/
_site_drafts.previous/
_site_report/

# Development only. Site generation never touches these.
node_modules/
node_modules.off/

# The compiled generators, about 100 MB each; build them with
# ./eleventy_binary/compile.sh. Do not commit them: site_generate.exe is over
# GitHub's 100 MB file limit, so the push is refused, and every rebuild would
# add another permanent copy to the history. To keep a copy off this machine,
# attach them to a GitHub Release instead.
site_generate
site_generate.exe
site_generate-arm64
site_generate-arm64.exe

# OS and editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp

# Tailwind
tailwindcss-linux-x64
tailwindcss-windows-x64.exe
# The page builder keeps a copy of every replaced document beside it. They are
# the author's own history, not content, and the build never reads them.
input_custom_post/*/.revisions/
